    "created_at": "2020-05-01T05:38:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-01T05:38:59Z",
    "body": "The browsing context group is not a good owner I think. It has no relation to a browsing session and can go away upon navigation due to COOP. I suppose we could go with a narrower variant of session that simply matches its lifetime, but with it still being a bit unclear when we want to replace the browsing context group in non-COOP scenarios I'd rather not.\r\n\r\nI think what I'll do for now is that in principle this kind of thing could be supported architecturally for all session buckets, but that we only fork the session bucket that backs `sessionStorage`.",
