    "created_at": "2020-05-01T07:00:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-01T07:00:05Z",
    "body": "fwiw, my use-case would be mostly taken care of if a page could access its session ID, and parent session ID, along with a way to get all the session IDs that were still potentially accessible (either active, or resurrectable somehow). Then developers could store session data in normal indexeddb, and manually delete old sessions.",
